\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Closing both directions at one vertex}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{In the [cellular torus](fdip-00SH), a period of one
retains a labeled loop in each direction and a face between
them. A cochain still has a vertex coefficient, two edge
coefficients and a face coefficient. The example with
links #{\qi} and #{\qj} in \ref{fdip-00SN} therefore
retains the order of transport despite having one vertex.
What are the determinant and the degree-zero part of the
inverse when these loop links range over all Hurwitz units?}
